{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-fake-exe/src/bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T01:06:19.374448Z","id":"54a769cb632947576c432d669e6b68854052cff5af948918a8bc301aad480a49","body":{"detail":"clax_bin's fallback runs scripts/stable-bin.sh once per process, and under cargo nextest each test is a process: each one copies target/debug/clax (105 MB) and runs shasum on it, about 0.4 s unloaded. In clax-cli this replaces running CARGO_BIN_EXE_clax in place at no cost. A bare 'cargo nextest run -p clax-mcp -p clax-hooks -p clax-cli -p clax-fake-exe' took 77.8 s, with the clax-mcp channel tests at 18-27 s each against 8-12 s with CLAX_TEST_BIN set. just test and scripts/quality_gates.sh set CLAX_TEST_BIN, so they never take this path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":65},"end":{"line":118},"content_hash":"c2ccf3cc72fcfce5467fb8b524f98c127429d98d2c8b12c16a3126cea40ed637"},"suggested_fix":"Look up the kept copy by the source's size and modification time before copying, or have nextest set CLAX_TEST_BIN through a setup script.","summary":"Without CLAX_TEST_BIN, every test process copies and hashes the 105 MB debug clax","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
